His Brittanic Majesty, the Right Honorable Sir Henry Mortimer Durand, G. C. M.
                    G., K. C. S. I., K. C. I. E., his Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary
                    near the Government of the United States;

And whereas the said Convention has been duly ratified on both parts, and the
                    ratifications of the two governments were exchanged in the City of Washington,
                    on the twelfth day of June, one thousand nine hundred and five;
